Subject: [PATCH] qemu: retain existing disk leases across an ACPI fake reboot

qemuProcessHandleShutdown marks fake-reboot CPU pauses with pausedShutdown.
The STOP handler deliberately retains disk leases in that case. Do not
resume/acquire those leases again when starting CPUs after system_reset:
virtlockd rejects the duplicate acquisition and the reboot worker kills
the domain. Ordinary starts and suspend/resume still acquire leases.

Reproduced with libvirt 12.8.0, QEMU 11.1.1 and lock_manager="lockd".
Upstream report: https://gitlab.com/libvirt/libvirt/-/work_items/892

---
--- a/src/qemu/qemu_process.c
+++ b/src/qemu/qemu_process.c
@@ -3451,8 +3451,12 @@ qemuProcessStartCPUs(virQEMUDriver *driver, virDomainObj *vm,
        return -1;
 
     VIR_DEBUG("Using lock state '%s'", NULLSTR(priv->lockState));
-    if (virDomainLockProcessResume(driver->lockManager, cfg->uri,
-                                   vm, priv->lockState) < 0) {
+    /* The STOP handler retains leases while pausedShutdown is set for a
+     * fake reboot. Reacquiring them would collide with this same domain's
+     * existing leases, causing an otherwise clean reboot to fail. */
+    if (!priv->pausedShutdown &&
+        virDomainLockProcessResume(driver->lockManager, cfg->uri,
+                                  vm, priv->lockState) < 0) {
         /* Don't free priv->lockState on error, because we need
          * to make sure we have state still present if the user
          * tries to resume again
